    "result_text": "Done. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: reject with **400** when an owner's email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nI followed the codebase's established binder-registered `Validator` pattern (the same one `PostcodeValidator` uses), which surfaces failures through the standard `@Valid` / `BindingResult` path that `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps to a 400.\n\n1. **New `DisposableEmailDomainValidator`** (`rest/controller/DisposableEmailDomainValidator.java`) \u2014 a single-responsibility Spring `Validator` for `OwnerFieldsDto`. It extracts the email's domain (case-insensitively, trimmed) and rejects the `email` field when it matches the blocklist. It's a no-op when no email is present, so the field stays optional.\n\n2. **Wired it into `OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added the import, constructor injection, and registered it on the existing owner binder alongside `ownerFieldsValidator` and `postcodeValidator`. This automatically covers both create (`POST`) and update (`PUT`), since both bind `ownerFieldsDto`.\n\nNo existing logic was duplicated \u2014 email canonicalization stays in `EmailNormalizer`, syntactic checks stay on the `@Email` constraint, and the new blocklist rule lives in its own small unit.",
